+### Consumed standalone Result execution material
+
+The original Result selection and predicate keep their full raw/native execution
+peak until the closed operation has been consumed in its concrete transaction.
+After its actual ACK exists, only their uniquely held decoder guards may be
+replaced by the actual outcome and effect-key receipt envelope. The command,
+W1 before proof, external priors and other domains remain held. The same sealed
+release reduces the already borrowed Input and Memory counters once; it neither
+registers the retained ACK again in Memory nor changes qualification or receipt
+ordering. EnsurePending, ordinary Task and Queue pending paths keep their
+existing material responsibility. Real copy caps and SQLite realloc bounds stay
+unchanged.
+
+
+The consumed Result exchange retains the complete still-live frozen command as
+a separate native/body allocation alongside the actual ACK envelope. If the new
+ACK is larger than the old selected row, its additional future-copy material
+is admitted to the same Task/Input/Memory allowance before receipt copies; a
+small old selection never makes that ACK free. The former post-business
+row-growth forecast is replaced only for this closed Result: it held no DTO,
+and each subsequent exact readback/qualified/coverage allocation is admitted
+at its own first copy. Original before bodies and actual State growth remain
+held and charged.
